Chapter: FactDiskRead
  cites Foreword chapter FactDisk
  cites Foreword chapter ImportGate
  cites Foreword chapter FactStore
  cites Foreword chapter Hamt
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe

 FactDisk is how the compiler reads a work out of the fact store: the
 quotation gate reaches it from `opening.codex`, and until this test
 nothing had ever run a line of it. The two fact-log disks that existed
 (`disk-facts-read.disk`, `disk-facts-load.disk`) hold a single kind-0
 entry each, so the source-definition decode path -- the entire reason the
 chapter exists -- had no fixture at all.

 The disk here is minted by `build/mint-factlog-fixture.ps1` from the
 SPECIFICATION: Foreword chapter FactLog for the sector layout, Foreword
 chapter SourceDefWire for the record format. It is deliberately NOT
 produced by running DiskFacts. A fixture written by the writer under test
 proves only that the reader agrees with its own writer, which is the
 failure `BrotliBeatsOpus` is about, and the reason the reverse direction
 gets written first.

 Three entries, in an order chosen to be adversarial:

   sector 2  kind 0   a five-character record that is NOT a definition
   sector 3  kind 30  an unsigned definition, hash abc123
   sector 4  kind 30  a signed definition, hash def456, signature aabb

 The kind-0 entry is FIRST on purpose. A walk that stopped at the first
 entry it could not decode would report zero works, and a walk that
 decoded it anyway would report three.

 The signed and unsigned records are both present because `fd-admit-work`
 routes them differently: an empty signature is OFFERED and a real one is
 PUBLISHED, and only the published one belongs in the bundle's signed map.
 A reader that published everything would look identical on a count.

 The last two lines are the supplement property. The compiler hands
 `store-read-bundle` the bundle it already built from the offered-works
 blob, so the disk must ADD to it and not replace it: a quotation the blob
 already satisfied has to still resolve afterwards.

 We say:

Section: Reading a fact back

  show-fact : Maybe Fact -> Text
  show-fact (m) =
    when m
     is None -> "absent"
     is Just (f) -> f.content & "/" & f.author & "/" & show (f.timestamp)

  show-signed : Maybe SignedFact -> Text
  show-signed (m) =
    when m
     is None -> "unpublished"
     is Just (s) -> s.signer-fingerprint & "/" & show (list-length (s.signature))

Section: A bundle that already holds something

  prior : Fact
  prior = Fact {
    hash = "zzz999",
    kind = DefinitionFact,
    content = "from the blob",
    author = "base",
    timestamp = 1
  }

Section: Body

  opening : [Console, Device.Block] Nothing = act
    fresh <- store-read-bundle bundle-empty
    print-line-uni ("count=" & show (fact-count (fresh.facts)))
    print-line-uni ("unsigned=" & show-fact (fact-load (fresh.facts) "abc123"))
    print-line-uni ("signed=" & show-fact (fact-load (fresh.facts) "def456"))
    print-line-uni ("published=" & show-signed (hamt-get (fresh.signed) "def456"))
    print-line-uni ("offered-not-published=" & show-signed (hamt-get (fresh.signed) "abc123"))
    supplemented <- store-read-bundle (bundle-offer bundle-empty prior)
    print-line-uni ("supplemented-count=" & show (fact-count (supplemented.facts)))
    print-line-uni ("prior-survives=" & show-fact (fact-load (supplemented.facts) "zzz999"))
  end
